  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe `popovertarget` attribute sets up an important relationship between the invoker button and a popover dialog. This relationship can also be hooked up with the `source` argument to `showPopover()`. If you call `showPopover()` on the popover without any arguments, though, that relationship is not created, even if the attribute is there.\n\nHaving set up the attribute, it is really easy to forget that argument when calling `showPopover()` via script. Even @tabatkins forgot to do this when creating some tests just last week.\n\nIf there is only one possible invoker on the page (i.e. only one element with its `popovertarget` set to this popover's ID), can we default the `source` argument to that element? (It would still be possible to set it to null explicitly, if that was actually intended.)",
